# Flutter commit hygiene (jarvis_app)

Before staging after `flutter pub get` / adding a plugin, **triage** desktop/mobile generated paths. Do not dump every `M` from `git status` into the commit.

## Usually commit (this repo tracks them)

When the diff **registers the new plugin** (real `+/-` lines, not empty):

- `pubspec.yaml`, `pubspec.lock`
- `macos/Flutter/GeneratedPluginRegistrant.swift`
- `windows/flutter/generated_plugin_registrant.cc`, `windows/flutter/generated_plugins.cmake`
- Platform permission / Info.plist / AndroidManifest edits you made on purpose

Same pattern as past plugin features (mic, attach, etc.).

## Often noise — inspect, then discard

- **`linux/flutter/generated_*`**: many plugins (e.g. `gal`) never appear here. Status may show `M` with **empty** `git diff` / same `git hash-object` as the index → CRLF or timestamp phantom. `git restore` those paths; do not commit.
- Empty or whitespace-only diffs on any `generated_plugin*` / `GeneratedPluginRegistrant*` → restore, do not stage.
- Auto-touched files unrelated to the feature with no meaningful content change → discard.

## Quick checks

```text
git diff --stat -- <path>          # empty but status M? → likely phantom
git hash-object <path>             # compare to: git ls-files -s <path>
Select-String / rg for the plugin name in linux vs windows/macos registrants
```

If linux (or another platform) has **no** plugin name and no real diff → leave it out of the commit.
